# Project conventions

This is a layered Python AI template. Keep code in the right layer:

- **app.py** — UI only. Streamlit (or FastAPI/CLI) entrypoint. No business logic; delegate to services.
- **src/services/** — Business logic and workflows. One module per feature (e.g. generate_text). Call integrations, not external APIs directly.
- **src/integrations/** — External systems only: LLM APIs, database, email, etc. No business rules.
- **src/prompts/** — App-level AI prompt templates (files or strings). Keep prompts out of service code when possible.
- **src/db/** — Optional: schema, migrations, or DB helpers. This template currently keeps SQLite in integrations.
- **src/utils/** — Shared helpers (formatting, parsing). No domain logic.
- **src/config.py** — Configuration and env vars. Single place for settings.

Prefer readable code. Add tests for important logic. Run tests with: `pytest` (from project root).
